==English==
===Etymology===
Hindustani [[नमस्कार]] / {{URchar|[[نمسکار]]}} ''namaskār'' < Sanskrit [[नमस्कार]] ''namaskāra'', from ''namas'': "to bow", "[[obeisance]]" and ''kāra'': "action".

===Interjection===
'''namaskar''' 

# respectful greetings

===Noun===
'''namaskar''' (countable)

# ''(Indian English)'' The use of the [[greet]]ing in which you put your hands together and then [[bow]] slightly.

===Related terms===
*[[namaste]]

